          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. State whether the following statements are True or False."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.299,
            0.104,
            0.883,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) A force is always required to change the speed of motion of an object."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.294,
            0.143,
            0.883,
            0.182
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Due to friction, the speed of the ball rolling on a flat ground increases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.289,
            0.182,
            0.883,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) There is no force between two charged objects placed at a small distance apart."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.225,
            0.883,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Two balloons rubbed with a woollen cloth are brought near each other. What would happen and why?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.269,
            0.883,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. When you drop a coin in a glass of water, it sinks, but when you place a bigger wooden block in water, it floats. Explain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.311,
            0.882,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. If a ball is thrown upwards, it slows down, stops momentarily, and then falls back to the ground. Name the forces acting on the ball and specify their directions. (i) During its upward motion (ii) During its downward motion (iii) At its topmost position"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
